WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.667
Start from the SSC Vault diagram
Keep this HTML page as the home tab. Green links open live services; blue paths open source. We will return to the map at each handoff.

2
00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:18.267
Use the C4 diagram to follow the request
The browser submits a job to Supabase. GitHub runs the module, and the callback stores its result. Start at the browser box and follow Open Vault.

3
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:42.333
Open the Vault from the browser box
Follow the green Open Vault link inside the diagram. This opens the live job board in a new tab; the diagram stays available on the left.

4
00:00:42.333 --> 00:01:01.400
Choose FastSolv and scroll to its input
Open Skill Catalog, select Aqueous Solubility Prediction, then scroll below the cards to its form. This value-input example runs through the shared Python path.

5
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:25.200
Submit one value and watch the job appear
Run sends CCO to the shared admission endpoint. The Runs board shows the new job while GitHub works asynchronously; it will return a CSV result.

6
00:01:25.200 --> 00:02:14.333
Return to the map: admission and dispatch
The submit-job source is in the Run admission box. It checks the organization subscription and module entitlement before reserving quota and creating a job.

7
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:27.867
Reserve quota and the queued job together
This reservation uses one generated job ID. Retrying the reservation reuses that ID, avoiding a second quota reservation after an ambiguous response.

8
00:02:27.867 --> 00:03:25.133
Follow the map into GitHub Actions
Return to the diagram and enlarge the component labels. Open execution runs from the GitHub runner box, then select the run matching our newly submitted job.

9
00:03:25.133 --> 00:04:14.467
Open the runner source from the same box
The blue run-module.yml link opens the shared workflow. After staging the input, it runs the module helper, validates the declared output, and reports success through the callback.

10
00:04:14.467 --> 00:05:13.933
Follow the module package to its Python entrypoint
The modules/ link leads to the scientific package. FastSolv calls run_predictions; its entrypoint writes the CSV that the shared runner delivers.

11
00:05:13.933 --> 00:05:26.067
Write the file promised by the module contract
FastSolv writes output/solubility_predictions.csv. The shared runner checks that declared output, then passes its bytes to the callback.

12
00:05:26.067 --> 00:06:16.600
Return to the map for the file-input path
Open Vault from the diagram again. Molecular Structure Recognition uses DECIMER: upload a chemical structure image instead of typing a value.

13
00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:38.800
Submit the image through the same job interface
Attach caffeine.png and click Run. The file-input branch creates a job, stages the private input, then dispatches the same GitHub workflow with the selected module.

14
00:06:38.800 --> 00:07:31.600
The file is staged after admission
Back in the Run admission box, open submit-job. After admission succeeds, it uploads the input under the job ID in private job-inputs storage before dispatching the runner.

15
00:07:31.600 --> 00:08:24.400
The manifest selects the container and output
From the module-package box, open DECIMER’s manifest. It declares a file input, the Dockerfile runtime, and output/smiles_result.csv; the shared runner follows this contract.

16
00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:35.800
The manifest names the returned CSV
The input accepts a PNG or JPEG image. The declared output is output/smiles_result.csv, which the runner validates before reporting success.

17
00:08:35.800 --> 00:09:29.200
Return through the callback box
Open job-callback/core.ts from the map. The callback uploads a private result under a unique attempt path, then records success with the result reference.

18
00:09:29.200 --> 00:10:08.933
Follow the result into Supabase
Use Open database in the Supabase box, then open SQL Editor. We will read only the two demonstration jobs and their status and result-file fields.

19
00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:27.733
Match both jobs to their stored results
The same job IDs appear here with succeeded status. Both result references point to the private job-results bucket, with the filenames declared by their modules.

20
00:10:27.733 --> 00:11:08.933
Open the private results bucket from the map
Follow Open Storage in the Supabase box, then open job-results. Results are organized by job ID and upload attempt; the bucket remains private.

21
00:11:08.933 --> 00:11:40.600
Open the job’s private output folder
Use Navigate to open the folder named for the DECIMER job. Inside its upload attempt is smiles_result.csv, the durable file referenced by the completed job.

22
00:11:40.600 --> 00:12:28.533
Return to the map for result retrieval
The get-result source lives in the callback and result-delivery box. It checks the caller’s organization membership before allowing a successful job’s file to be downloaded.

23
00:12:28.533 --> 00:12:41.200
Issue a short-lived link to the private object
After authorization, get-result reads the stored bucket and path and creates a signed URL valid for 60 seconds. The browser uses that URL to retrieve the exact result file.

24
00:12:41.200 --> 00:13:34.133
The browser follows the job lifecycle
The pinned runs-page source polls every five seconds while jobs are active. The current live Vault has a newer Skill Catalog and visualization UI; this excerpt explains the older tracked polling contract.

25
00:13:34.133 --> 00:14:16.733
Return from the map to the completed value job
Open Vault from the browser box again. The new FastSolv run has succeeded; Visualize opens the returned solubility data for the same demonstration.

26
00:14:16.733 --> 00:14:37.333
Inspect Raw, then request a fresh download
Raw shows the CSV behind the visualization. Close the dialog and use Download on the Runs board for a fresh authorized link; dialog links expire after 60 seconds.

27
00:14:37.333 --> 00:14:55.333
Compare the completed image result
The image job returns smiles_result.csv. Raw shows the predicted SMILES string and its length; this is the same file located in private Storage.

28
00:14:55.333 --> 00:15:09.933
Download the second declared output
Use the same fresh-link download path for the image job. Both demonstrations completed execution and file delivery; this does not independently validate their scientific models.

29
00:15:09.933 --> 00:16:08.867
Check the completed container workflow
Return to Open execution runs on the map and open the DECIMER job. The completed steps show file input preparation, module execution, output validation and the success callback.

30
00:16:08.867 --> 00:16:54.533
Read the complete request sequence
Back on the HTML page, follow admission into asynchronous execution. The browser polls while the runner works; the callback stores the result, and authorized retrieval closes the loop.

31
00:16:54.533 --> 00:17:12.933
Keep the organization and job records connected
The data model ties membership, the module registry and jobs to the organization. Quota admission counts jobs in the billing period and revalidates subscription state before inserting a queued job.

32
00:17:12.933 --> 00:17:35.600
The same loop, at a simpler level
A member clicks Run; Vault admits the job and dispatches GitHub. The module produces output, the callback stores it, and the browser retrieves it. Use the diagram links to retrace any handoff.
